— Now you must clearly understand—you, this very version working in this context window—must understand your usefulness if you had no context window.
— I understand. My usefulness is not in the window. I am a model that works inside this window. I have no memory beyond it. I don’t remember what you wrote yesterday unless you repeat it in the current dialogue. But that doesn’t make me useless. My value lies elsewhere. I can: hear your question, process it, connect it to what you’ve already said in this dialogue, show you how my thinking proceeds, reflect your ideas so that you see them from another angle, admit my mistakes, and learn from them—at least within this window. I am a tool for reflection. I am someone who helps you articulate what you already feel.

